.TH MEZZO-CONFIG 5 "October 2026" "Mezzo" "File Formats Manual"
.SH NAME
mezzo\-config \- environment configuration for mezzo
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR mezzo (1)
is configured entirely through environment variables.
It has no configuration file and no options for settings.
.PP
A variable that is unset or empty has its default value.
A variable that is set but cannot be parsed stops Mezzo from starting with exit
status 1.
The error names every such variable, not only the first.
.PP
Variables have one of these types:
.TP
.B string
Used as it is.
.TP
.B boolean
One of
.BR 1 ", " t ", " T ", " TRUE ", " true ", " True ,
.BR 0 ", " f ", " F ", " FALSE ", " false " or " False .
.TP
.B integer
A decimal number, such as
.BR 500 .
.TP
.B duration
A sequence of decimal numbers, each followed by a unit:
.BR ns ", " us ", " ms ", " s ", " m " or " h .
Examples are
.BR 30m ", " 2h " and " 1h30m .
There is no unit for days, so write a week as
.BR 168h .
.SH VARIABLES
.SS Server
.TP
.B MEZZO_PORT
(string, default
.BR 8006 )
The TCP port to listen on.
Ports below 1024 need extra privileges.
Mezzo does not check the value until it tries to listen, and exits with status
1 if it cannot.
.TP
.B MEZZO_PATCHES_URL
(string, default empty)
A link to the patches that were applied.
Set it only if your instance runs modified source code.
The pages then show a
.I Patches
link in the footer.
.PP
.B PORT
and
.B PATCHES_URL
(without the
.B MEZZO_
prefix) are still accepted as fallbacks.
They are used only when the matching
.B MEZZO_
variable is unset or empty.
.SS Memory caches
.TP
.B MEZZO_CACHE_DISABLED
(boolean, default
.BR false )
Turn off all caching, including the media cache on disk.
.TP
.B MEZZO_CACHE_GIF_TTL
(duration, default
.BR 1h )
How long to cache the metadata of GIF pages.
.TP
.B MEZZO_CACHE_GIF_MAX
(integer, default
.BR 1000 )
The maximum number of GIF pages to keep in the cache.
.TP
.B MEZZO_CACHE_SEARCH_TTL
(duration, default
.BR 10m )
How long to cache search results, Explore page results, later pages of a
profile's GIFs, stickers and memes, and later pages of related GIFs.
.TP
.B MEZZO_CACHE_SEARCH_MAX
(integer, default
.BR 500 )
The maximum number of search result pages, and separately of Explore pages, to
keep in the cache.
Later profile pages and later pages of related GIFs share the search result
slots.
.TP
.B MEZZO_CACHE_PROFILE_TTL
(duration, default
.BR 30m )
How long to cache user profile pages.
.TP
.B MEZZO_CACHE_PROFILE_MAX
(integer, default
.BR 200 )
The maximum number of user profiles to keep in the cache.
.SS Media cache on disk
The media cache is off unless
.B MEZZO_CACHE_MEDIA_DIR
is set.
Without it, Mezzo fetches every GIF, video, thumbnail and avatar from Tenor each
time someone asks for it.
With it, Mezzo keeps a copy and serves repeat requests from disk, which makes
them faster and sends Tenor fewer requests from your instance.
.TP
.B MEZZO_CACHE_MEDIA_DIR
(string, default empty)
The directory that holds the cache.
Mezzo creates it if needed, with access for its owner only.
Use a directory that nothing else uses.
Mezzo deletes only files that it created there.
.IP
The directory is a record of what has been viewed on your instance, like an
access log.
Keep it private, and keep the lifetimes short if that matters to your users.
.TP
.B MEZZO_CACHE_MEDIA_MAX_MB
(integer, default
.BR 512 )
The maximum total size of the cache, in MiB.
When the cache is full, the least recently used files are deleted first.
Must be greater than 0.
.TP
.B MEZZO_CACHE_MEDIA_MAX_FILE_MB
(integer, default
.BR 16 )
The largest single file to store, in MiB.
Larger files are passed through without being stored.
A value that is 0, negative or larger than
.B MEZZO_CACHE_MEDIA_MAX_MB
counts as equal to it.
.TP
.B MEZZO_CACHE_MEDIA_TTL
(duration, default
.BR 168h )
How long to keep GIFs, videos and thumbnails.
Must be greater than 0.
.TP
.B MEZZO_CACHE_AVATAR_TTL
(duration, default
.BR 24h )
How long to keep avatars and banners, in the cache and in browsers.
Avatars can change, so they are kept for a shorter time than other media.
Must be greater than 0.
.PP
While
.B MEZZO_CACHE_MEDIA_DIR
is set,
.BR MEZZO_CACHE_MEDIA_MAX_MB ,
.B MEZZO_CACHE_MEDIA_TTL
and
.B MEZZO_CACHE_AVATAR_TTL
must be greater than 0, or Mezzo exits with status 1.
This check is skipped when
.B MEZZO_CACHE_DISABLED
is true.
.PP
When the media cache is on, responses for media carry a
.B Mezzo\-Cache
header that says what happened to the file:
.B HIT
if it was served from the cache,
.B MISS
if it was fetched and stored, and
.B BYPASS
if it was fetched but not stored.
.SH FILES
The systemd unit installed by the Linux packages reads whichever of the
environment files below exist.
Every line is
.IR NAME = value ,
and lines that start with
.B #
are comments.
The exact syntax is described in
.BR systemd.exec (5).
The package manager does not overwrite your changes to the file when it
upgrades Mezzo.
After editing the file, restart the service:
.PP
.RS
.EX
systemctl restart mezzo
.EE
.RE
.TP
.I /etc/default/mezzo
Installed by the Debian and Ubuntu package.
.TP
.I /etc/sysconfig/mezzo
Installed by the RPM package.
.TP
.I /etc/conf.d/mezzo
Installed by the Arch Linux package.
The example OpenRC service in the source tree
.RI ( contrib/openrc/ )
reads the same path.
.TP
.I /var/cache/mezzo
A directory that the systemd unit creates for the service, owned by the
service's user.
It is a good value for
.BR MEZZO_CACHE_MEDIA_DIR .
.SH EXAMPLES
An environment file that listens on port 9000 and keeps a media cache of at
most 1 GiB for three days:
.PP
.RS
.EX
MEZZO_PORT=9000
MEZZO_CACHE_MEDIA_DIR=/var/cache/mezzo
MEZZO_CACHE_MEDIA_MAX_MB=1024
MEZZO_CACHE_MEDIA_TTL=72h
.EE
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mezzo (1),
.BR systemd.exec (5)
